<a target="_new" href="
http://rpgvault.ign.com/articles/359/359987p1.html">Morrowind Preview</a><br>
RPG Vault&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
5/22/2002 7:30:14 AM<P>
RPG Vault has added their first impressions of Morrowind. Here is a bit of what they thought:<p>
"Probably the most telling aspect of Morrowind s far is that the hours of play went by in a flash. The time spent playing has felt effortless. Given that Bethesda's developers have publicly speculated that there could be 500 hours of gameplay, it's no wonder people can barely contain their excitement."<br>
<hr>
<a target="_new" href="
http://www.rpgdot.com/index.php?hsaction=10053&ID=316">Morrowind Preview Part 3 </a><br>
RPGDot&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
4/29/2002 6:54:20 AM<P>
RPGDot has added part 3 of their Morrowind preview. Here is a little bit about the roleplaying:<p>
"So all we want to say about character generation is: it is extremely well done, woven into the game and lets you, within the boundaries set for beginning characters, create an avatar that reflects the role you want to play."<br>
<hr>
<a target="_new" href="
http://www.rpgdot.com/index.php?hsaction=10053&ID=311">Morrowind Preview Part 2 </a><br>
RPGDot&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
4/25/2002 10:03:03 AM<P>
RPGDot has added the second part of their preview to the website. Here is a bit of what they had to say:<p>
"The developers said it over and over again: the world of Morrowind is huge. They never answered HOW huge it is, and this is for a good reason. We think that even for those who created it, this is impossible to answer."<br>
<hr>
<a target="_new" href="
http://www.rpgdot.com/index.php?hsaction=10053&ID=307">Morrowind Preview Part 1</a><br>
RPGDot&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
4/23/2002 7:51:14 AM<P>
RPGDot has posted their first part of the Morrwind preview.<p>
"But neither graphics nor the RPG system are the most impressive things in Morrowind - it's the whole package. Whoever was responsible for the design decisions that have been made over the years, has done an outstanding job. Morrowind will be one of the few games where things seem to "snap together". Why it is so - we will discuss that in the upcoming parts of our preview."<br>
<hr>
<a target="_new" href="
http://rpgvault.ign.com/features/previews/morrowind.shtml">Elder Scrolls III: Morrowind Preview</a><br>
RPG Vault&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;
4/11/2002 7:00:13 AM<P>
RPG Vault has completed their preview of Morrowind. Here is a bit of what to expect:<p>
"Regardless of current code issues, Bethesda has clearly conceived a fine RPG with the potential for very wide appeal. Here are just some of the interesting facts about the third Elder Scrolls game that should get fans, old and new alike, lining up at their local software stores in a few weeks."<br>
